  "implemented": [
    "Existing directly owned payer journal notes can recover spending authority below an authenticated native history floor",
    "Recovery still requires the original encrypted journal and derived receiving/spending credentials, plus membership at the recorded position in the current canonical note tree",
    "Canonical pool/code/factory/custody, active math/value rules, exact roots/count and a revocable same-node publication lease remain mandatory",
    "The imported floor clock comes from its independently verified finalized QC, survives checkpoint reopen and refuses altered captured head metadata; commit dates and wall clocks remain unused",
    "Native timestamp conversion occurs only when reading the clock; checkpoint trust and import acceptance rules are unchanged",
    "Retained creation histories keep their original verification path; incoming receipt imports and operator credit validation are unchanged",
    "Selection, reservations, cancellation checks and purchase reconciliation use the same recovered note-opening path",
    "No new receipt, purchase timing, invoice validity or purchased traffic capacity is inferred from current membership",
    "Existing journal format and key derivation are preserved; no migration, seed reset, new key export or counter reset occurs"
  ],
